  "limitations": [
    "Beta.2 binds remediated source 6d4d0a05, stock OMP 18.12.6, published model 81f924d4 and strict-origin config 751d22dc. Full council on reviewed F and verified localized F2 remediation is bound; fresh RTX 5090 public-route acceptance and final evidence pins remain separate. Root files stay on the historical candidate until the lead lane pin.",
    "The client is unmodified upstream OMP and has no appliance commands; supported installation/lifecycle routes measure model/image identities before launch. Manually bypassed identity-asserting launches are not certified.",
    "Checkpoint schema 3 uses isolated /checkpoints-v013. Never mount, scan, import or migrate v0.12.x roots; keep old roots untouched for rollback and replay prior sessions from OMP transcripts. No quota-GC safety promise is made for an unsupported operator-selected legacy root.",
    "Strict origin authentication requires a checkpoint root and API key at least 32 bytes. MACs prove origin/content, not monotonic freshness: a filesystem writer can replay an older authentic generation. No anti-replay authority is claimed.",
    "Checkpointing is best effort. A crash or expired graceful wait can lose unpublished acceleration state. Native import/victim proof performs finite payload I/O/hash work on the device worker and may delay decode; removing the Responses-lock cycle does not remove all worker I/O.",
    "Within one API-key principal, prompt_cache_key names a session capability; use unique high-entropy keys and do not share that principal among mutually untrusted clients.",
    "JSON-schema output and 128-character Chat/Responses tool names are qualified on the rebased RTX 5090. Carried natives reject schema output and retain 64-character names; client/public-route acceptance is separate.",
    "The strict RTX 5090 profile has 146368 automatic BF16 KV tokens, 131072 context, DFlash2 K=7, two active lanes plus two extra device-state slots, and 180-second pending timeout. Two requests run together only while prompts/output reservations fit; no constant-batch-two, universal warm reuse or prefill/decode fairness guarantee.",
    "Carried native v0.6.11 RTX 4090 and v0.6.3 RTX 3090 packages/model eec39564 remain unchanged, GPU-UUID-bound and sequential on port 18082. Main reports their OMP 18.12.6 windows remain valid; actual receipts/pins still must be bound. Rebased 24 GB packages and Windows K6 execution remain independently qualified v0.13.1 work.",
    "Superseded durable-owner metadata and authenticated session-gate churn can retain capacity/metadata. Stale publication may leave bounded orphan-generation work. These residuals and workflow base-receipt cross-checking are deferred to v0.13.1, not claimed fixed by the localized remediation.",
    "Powered quality/leak/global output parity, historical OMP parallel/fanout/warm-arrival latency, and full G2 after canonical serialization/F2 are not re-measured. EXP-097 stays bound to its measured c2dbcbae source/model, not this final runtime.",
    "Multi-GPU inference, simultaneous native serving, multi-tenant operation, priority guarantees and silent cloud fallback are unsupported. macOS remains preview; Linux evidence is WSL2-scoped. RTX 4090 retains no supported rollback target on its two-GPU lineage; RTX 3090 retains its actual qualified predecessor."
  ],
